--TEST--
`Core\Response::sendFile`'s path is a sink and refuses a tainted argument, where the same response's `text` body takes one — a path component directs the resolver and a body's octets are framed — `rule:security/sink-predicate`, `rule:security/response-body-is-one-typed-member`, spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/sink-predicate`'s table puts a filesystem path component on
// the instruction side -- `..` and the separators direct the resolver -- so a
// path the request itself chose is the traversal that sends back whatever this
// program was granted. A `tainted` one is refused before it runs.
tainted string $chosen = "page.html";

Core\Response::sendFile($chosen);

// And the other side of § 4's table on the same class, so this file asserts a
// line rather than a member: the text body takes a tainted argument freely,
// because `nosniff` is on by default and its octets are framed by
// `Content-Length` rather than becoming an instruction to anything.
Core\Response::text($chosen);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:8:25
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
